# Test SSH Key Pair for Boot Tests

This key pair is a TEST FIXTURE, not a secret. It is used by scripts/boot-test
to authenticate SSH connections during testing. The image trusts the public key
via authorizedKeys.

Files:
- test-ssh.pub: Public key (trusted by the image, committed)
- test-ssh: Private key (used by test script, committed)

These keys are intentionally committed because:
1. They are test-only fixtures, not production secrets
2. Both keys must be available: public at build time, private at test time
3. The keys have no value outside this test harness

To regenerate (if needed):
  ssh-keygen -t ed25519 -N '' -f test-ssh -C "golconda-boot-test"
  Then update nix/default.nix to read the new public key.
